{sov: Notes}
80s Pop Landmark: Features Bruce Hornsby's iconic, two-handed, syncopated
piano riff in G Major / A Dorian.

Main Loop: The core verse progression walks down through Am7 - C - G - F,
utilizing the flat-VII (F) chord for a modal pop feel.

Chorus Lift: The chorus opens up by leading directly with the G - F - C
cadence before returning to the familiar verse walkdown loop.

Improvisation: Piano and guitar solos freely navigate A Dorian and G Major
pentatonic scales over the steady 2-bar progression frame.
{eov}